# Scoped to setup/server/Dockerfile, so the repo-root .dockerignore is left
# alone.
#
# **Everything out, and what the build reads let back in by name.** A list
# of what to leave out was always one file short: `.pytest_cache/` is rewritten
# by every test run, a stray file at the root is picked up the moment it
# appears, and either one changed the context -- so the source copy missed the
# cache and all three images rebuilt although nothing in them had changed. An
# allow-list means a new directory in the tree cannot do that.
#
# .git is let in for the `version` stage alone, which mounts it rather than
# copying it: it changes on every git command, and there it costs one cheap
# step. The wheel stage copies only the package and its metadata files.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!MANIFEST.in
!siliconcompiler/
!setup/server/
!.git

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
